[[ plugin_summary ]]

A plugin for [Heinzelmännchen](https://github.com/[[ heinzel_owner ]]/heinzel), the open-source, AI-driven operating system for
product development teams.


## Install

With Heinzelmännchen installed (`uv tool install git+https://github.com/[[ heinzel_owner ]]/heinzel`):

```bash
hz system plugin add git+https://github.com/[[ github_owner ]]/[[ project_name ]]             # shows what it installs
hz system plugin add git+https://github.com/[[ github_owner ]]/[[ project_name ]] --confirm   # installs it
```

Pin a version with `@vX.Y.Z`. Running `hz system plugin add` again upgrades; `hz system plugin remove [[ project_name ]]` removes it.

## Use

```bash
hz [[ plugin_name ]] info                 # this plugin, its version and the Heinzelmännchen it runs on
hz [[ plugin_name ]] hello --name Ada     # a submodule collapsed into a command
hz [[ plugin_name ]] info --json          # every command speaks JSON, for scripts and agents
hz system info                  # includes a section contributed by this plugin
```

## Documentation

[docs/plugins/[[ project_name ]]/index.md](docs/plugins/[[ project_name ]]/index.md) is this plugin's page: what it
brings in every head, its settings, credentials, themes and recordings, generated from the installed plugin by
`hz system plugin docs build` (`make fix` writes it, `make check` fails while it is missing or stale).
`make docs-record` records the scenes of [docs/scenes.toml](docs/scenes.toml) beside it, and `make docs-site` builds
the site the Docs workflow publishes on release.

## Develop

```bash
make setup     # everything the build needs, and the git hooks; you need only git, make and uv
make doctor    # what is missing, and the command that fixes it
make check     # lint, types, unit + integration tests
make test-e2e  # installs Heinzelmännchen with uv and adds this checkout as a plugin
```

The modules live in `src/[[ package_name ]]/`. Read [AGENTS.md](AGENTS.md) and
[docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md](docs/CODING_STANDARDS.md) before changing them; the reviewer agents and hooks in
`.claude/` enforce them.

## Release

`make release` (or Actions → **Prepare release** → Run workflow) opens a release pull request on GitHub that merges itself
once CI is green; merging tags and publishes. The version comes
from conventional commits, the changelog from git-cliff; the GitHub release carries the wheel, the sdist and
provenance attestations. `main` changes only through pull requests.

Add the topic `heinzel-plugin` to the GitHub repository so `hz system plugin search` lists the plugin.

## Stay current

This repository was generated from Heinzelmännchen's copier template ([[ heinzel_version ]]). `make update-template` pulls in the
latest standards, tooling and CI from Heinzelmännchen.
